# Trivy IaC findings to suppress.
# Format: one Trivy check ID per line.
# Add a comment above each entry explaining why it is suppressed.

# The Key Vault has no network ACL by default: cloud-init on every node reads its secrets through
# the public endpoint behind the NAT Gateway, and an operator applying from outside Azure must
# write them. key_vault.network_access = "Private" is the hardened path, with a private endpoint
# the consumer provides.
AVD-AZU-0013

# The OIDC issuer storage account serves public documents by design (the discovery document and
# JWKS Entra reads), so it has no network rules. The blob CSI account is open only when the
# consumer sets blob_csi.network_access = "Public".
AVD-AZU-0012
